§§ `8 מבנה שבוע העבודה`

-- akn:art_8 The heading of §8.

-- (א): the parties give notice on signing, under §13 of the Collective
-- Agreements Law, 1957, that this section ends on 31.8.2017; they may
-- agree before then to extend it. ¶2: the Oz agreement goes on by law.
-- (ב): what it says was agreed on 5.2.2014, and that takes nothing from
-- §2(א). The agreement of 14.3.2018 (§23) says §§8 and 11 did not end.
@ref akn:art_8__para_a akn:art_8__para_a/p2 akn:art_8__para_b
`the day §8 of 26.6.2014 was given notice to end` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2017
`§8 of 26.6.2014 was agreed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 2 2014


-- (ג): §9 of the Oz agreement is replaced. The new §9, as far as it
-- changes the old (oz-founding-9, imported):
-- (א) a full position is 40 weekly hours, as before;
-- (ב) a full-position teacher's hours are 8:00–15:30 on Sunday to Thursday
-- and 8:00–12:45 on the short day (Friday, or Saturday or Sunday in a
-- non-Jewish sector), by the bell schedule — where they were 8:00–16:00
-- and 8:00–13:00;
-- (ב1) a teaching employee's hours count from his clock-in, not before
-- 7:45; (ב2) at his request before a school year or a half of it, the
-- principal may open his day before 8:00, not before 7:00; the hours count
-- from the clock-in, not before that hour, are placed as teaching-support
-- hours, and the day ends earlier as much;
-- (ג) the morning prayer, as before, not before 7:00, the day ending
-- earlier as much;
-- (ד) one whose free day is not the short day completes the 40 hours from
-- 15:30 to 16:15 on Sunday to Thursday and/or from 13:00 to 13:45 on the
-- short day — where it was 16:00–17:00 and 13:00–14:00;
-- (ה) in special cases the principal, with the teachers' committee, may set
-- other hours for those cases only, not the number of hours or their
-- make-up; (ה1) a teacher who needs special facilities not free between
-- 8:00 and 16:15 may work after 16:15, no more than 9 hours in a day;
-- (ו)–(י): 24 frontal, 6 individual and 10 teaching-support hours, the mix,
-- no conversion, and a substitution hour in a support hour's place — the
-- old §9(ו)–(י) word for word, whose rules stand (oz-founding-9);
-- (י1) the principal and a teacher may agree a plan of fewer support hours
-- in earlier months and more in months of heavier work, no month reduced
-- for more than one month heavier, within 9 hours a day and 43 a week; the
-- month's salary does not change, the reduced months' pay being an advance;
-- the teacher signs his consent;
-- (יא) for the weekly presence of one who works fewer than 8 weekly hours
-- in a day, an hour is a teaching period as the Ministry and the school's
-- bell schedule set it — where it was 60 minutes; (יב) the teacher's
-- duties in the school and by the timetable stand; (יג) §§26(י) and 30(ג)
-- are cancelled, and "(שעות של 60 דקות)" is struck from the work-week
-- tables of annexes א', א'3, ב', ב'3, ג' and ג'3.
@ref akn:art_8__para_c
