            (LIST `a long day is free`, `the short day is free`)
    AND `the length of the Oz working day, as amended on 26.6.2014` `a long working day` PLUS `the completion window of a day, as amended on 26.6.2014` AT MOST `the long day section 5(ב) lets an approved agreement set`
    AND `the length of the Oz working day, as amended on 26.6.2014` `the short working day` PLUS `the completion window of a day, as amended on 26.6.2014` AT MOST `the longest working day section 2 allows` TRUE
    AND `the most hours (ה1) and (י1) allow in a day` AT MOST `the long day section 5(ב) lets an approved agreement set`
    AND `the most hours (י1) allows in a week` AT MOST `the longest working week section 3 allows`
#ASSERT `the new section 9's windows keep sections 2, 3 and 5`

-- (יא): an hour of presence is a teaching period now, no longer 60 minutes.
`an hour of Oz presence is 60 minutes, as amended on 26.6.2014` MEANS FALSE

#ASSERT `minutes in an hour of Oz presence` EQUALS 60

-- (ד): §22 of the Oz agreement is replaced. The new §22, as far as it
-- changes the old (oz-founding-22, imported): (א) a principal's position
-- base is 40 weekly hours, as before; (ב) his hours are 8:00–15:30/16:15
-- on Sunday to Thursday and 8:00–12:45/13:45 on the short day — where they
-- were 8:00–16:00/17:00 and 8:00–13:00/14:00; (ג) one whose free day is
-- not the short day completes the 40 from 15:30 to 16:15 and/or from 13:00
-- to 13:45; (ד) 3 to 6 of the 40 are frontal teaching, by the Ministry's
-- guidelines, and the rest management and evaluation; (ה) his role hours
-- are done in the school; (ו) a mother principal of a child under 14 is
-- spared 2.4 management hours; (ז) the age reduction stands; (ח) for his
-- weekly presence an hour is a teaching period by the Ministry and the
-- bell schedule — where it was 60 minutes — and the rest of §22 stands.
-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: the new §22 sets
-- the hours of a school principal, a management post §30(א)(5) leaves out
-- of the law (convention instruments.hours-law-teaching).
@ref akn:art_8__para_d
`the Oz principal's position base, as amended on 26.6.2014` MEANS 40

#ASSERT `the Oz principal's position base, as amended on 26.6.2014` EQUALS `the Oz principal's position base`

GIVEN d IS A `day of an Oz principal's week`, `he completes that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hour an Oz principal's working day ends, as amended on 26.6.2014` d `he completes that day` IS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `a long day of the principal's week` THEN IF `he completes that day` THEN 16.25 ELSE 15.5
    WHEN `the short day of the principal's week` THEN IF `he completes that day` THEN 13.75 ELSE 12.75

#ASSERT `the hour an Oz principal's working day ends` `a long day of the principal's week` TRUE MINUS `the hour an Oz principal's working day ends, as amended on 26.6.2014` `a long day of the principal's week` TRUE EQUALS 0.75

#ASSERT `the management hours a mother principal is spared` EQUALS 2.4

§§ `9 הערכת מורים`

-- akn:art_9 The heading of §9.

-- (א): further to §19, from תשע"ה teachers are evaluated in every school,
-- whether it joined the reform or not, by the Ministry's initial model
-- agreed with the organisation at the meeting of 6.3.2014 (as summed up on
-- 11.3.2014, with the model); naming them changes not their standing.
@ref akn:art_9__para_a
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `26.6.2014 amendment action`
DECIDE `evaluating the teachers in every school in` y IS
    IF y AT LEAST `the school year 5775`
    THEN PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
         MUST  `evaluate the teachers by the initial model`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (ב): from תשע"ד, §35 of the Oz agreement (with all its sub-sections) is
-- cancelled. (ג): that takes nothing from §20 — a teacher on the reform's
-- terms may gather credit points from the evaluation of תשע"ה on, toward a
-- promotion grade.
@ref akn:art_9__para_b akn:art_9__para_c
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 35 stands for school year, as amended on 26.6.2014,` y IF
    y LESS THAN `the school year 5774`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      t IS AN `Oz grant teacher`
      `teachers evaluated above him` IS A NUMBER
      `the school's teachers` IS A NUMBER
      `the May indices` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the evaluation grant under section 35, as amended on 26.6.2014` y t `teachers evaluated above him` `the school's teachers` `the May indices` IS
    IF `section 35 stands for school year, as amended on 26.6.2014,` y
    THEN `the evaluation grant under section 35` y t `teachers evaluated above him` `the school's teachers` `the May indices`
    ELSE 0

`credit points toward promotion count from` MEANS `the school year 5775`

-- (ד): the teachers on the reform's terms in תשע"ג are owed a one-time
-- grant of 666 for a full position; one part-time, or employed for part of
-- the year (unpaid leave or sabbatical in part of it among them), its part
-- by his position and by the part of the year (September to June) he was
-- employed. (ז): none to one employed in תשע"ג (27.8.2012–20.6.2013) as a
-- substitute only, or on unpaid leave or sabbatical above 6 months of it.
-- The shape is §35(ו)'s, for the next year (oz-founding-35).
@ref akn:art_9__para_d akn:art_9__para_g
`the 2014 grant for a full position` MEANS 666
`the months of the 2014 grant's year` MEANS 10

GIVEN t IS AN `Oz grant teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2014 grant for the school year 5773` t IS
    IF      NOT t's `on the reform's terms` EQUALS `off the Oz reform`
        AND NOT t's `a substitute only`
        AND NOT t's `months on unpaid leave or sabbatical` `is above` 6
    THEN `an Oz grant pro rata` `the 2014 grant for a full position` (t's `position share`)
             (min 1 (t's `months employed from September to June` DIVIDED BY `the months of the 2014 grant's year`))
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT `the 2014 grant for the school year 5773` (`a reform teacher at` 0.5 `for` 10 `months, with` 0 `on maternity leave and` 0 `on leave`) EQUALS 333
#ASSERT `the 2014 grant for the school year 5773` (`a reform teacher at` 1 `for` 3 `months, with` 0 `on maternity leave and` 7 `on leave`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the months of the 2014 grant's year` EQUALS `the months of section 35(ו)'s year`

-- (ה): the grant is not in the base of the hour value, severance or a
-- percentage supplement, and no training-fund contribution is made on it;
-- (ו): 5% employer's and 5% teacher's contributions to a pension fund for
-- benefits — §35(ז)–(ח)'s rule for its grants (imported).
-- not weighed against `the Severance Pay Law`: (ה) leaves the grant out of
-- the wage severance is computed on; which components count, §13 sends to
-- the regulations, which compute that wage by the collective agreement
-- that applies; it sets no floor of its own beside it.
@ref akn:art_9__para_e akn:art_9__para_f
GIVEN p IS A `what an Oz salary component counts for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2014 grant counts for` p IF
    `the section 35 grants count for` p

`the employer's pension contribution rate on the 2014 grant` MEANS `the employer's pension contribution rate on a section 35 grant`
`the teacher's pension deduction rate on the 2014 grant` MEANS `the teacher's pension deduction rate on a section 35 grant`

#ASSERT NOT `the 2014 grant counts for` `Oz severance pay under the Severance Pay Law`
#ASSERT `the employer's pension contribution rate on the 2014 grant` EQUALS 5%

-- (ח): paid in the salary for August 2014. (ט): no grant for תשע"ד.
@ref akn:art_9__para_h akn:art_9__para_i
`paying the 2014 grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the grant of 666 in the salary for August 2014`
    WITHIN DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2014) MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the bagrut amendment agreement was signed on`

`a grant is paid for the school year 5774 under the 2014 amendment` MEANS FALSE

§§ `10 שינויים בשכר מנהלי בתי ספר`

-- akn:art_10 The heading of §10.

-- (א): notwithstanding §24(ב), from תשע"ד the transition supplement is in
-- the base of the management allowance paid to principals.
@ref akn:art_10__para_a
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, s IS A `supplement on an Oz principal's salary`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transition supplement is in the base of, as amended on 26.6.2014,` y s IF
        `the transition supplement is in the base of` s
    OR  (y AT LEAST `the school year 5774` AND s EQUALS `the principal's management allowance`)

#ASSERT NOT `the transition supplement is in the base of` `the principal's management allowance`
#ASSERT `the transition supplement is in the base of, as amended on 26.6.2014,` `the school year 5774` `the principal's management allowance`

-- (ב): from תשע"ד, §§24(ד), 24(ה), 24(ו) and 31(א) are void: the Oz
-- LaTmura supplement for principals, 30%, and its part-application rates.
@ref akn:art_10__para_b
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A `Oz staff member`, e IS A `extent of the Oz reform`, c IS A `Oz principal's salary components`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Oz LaTmura supplement for principals, as amended on 26.6.2014,` y m e c IS
    IF y LESS THAN `the school year 5774`
    THEN `the Oz LaTmura supplement for principals for` m e c
    ELSE 0

§§ `11 הרפורמה בבחינות הבגרות`

-- akn:art_11 The heading of §11.

-- (א): notice, as §8(א), that this section ends on 31.8.2017 (kept in force
-- by the agreement of 14.3.2018, §23).
@ref akn:art_11__para_a
`the day §11 of 26.6.2014 was given notice to end` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2017

-- (ב): the organisation accepts the matriculation reform as presented on
-- 5.2.2014, save the annex's "second stage", and undertakes to cooperate
-- fully in carrying it out, the school's own assessment among it; that is
-- no consent to dismissing teachers or cutting their positions for it.
@ref akn:art_11__para_b
`cooperating in the bagrut reform` MEANS
    PARTY `the secondary teachers' organisation`
    MUST  `cooperate fully in carrying out the bagrut reform`

`the organisation consents to dismissals for the bagrut reform` MEANS FALSE

-- (ג): no change in the pay for guiding pupils in matriculation subjects
-- (research projects and performance tasks among them), for the subjects
-- and tasks paid before the signing. (ד): no change in the conditions of
-- the bagrut-preparation allowances, by hours or by percent, subject to
-- (ה): where the external exam (about 70% of the material) and the
-- school's assessment (about 30%) fall in different school years, 70% of
-- the subject's allowance is paid in the year the class sits the external
-- exam and 30% in the year of the school's assessment.
@ref akn:art_11__para_c akn:art_11__para_d akn:art_11__para_e
`the external exam's share of the bagrut-preparation allowance` MEANS 70%
`the school assessment's share of the bagrut-preparation allowance` MEANS 30%

GIVEN `the subject's bagrut-preparation allowance` IS A NUMBER
      `the external exam is this year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the school assessment is this year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the bagrut-preparation allowance paid this year, by §11(ה)` `the subject's bagrut-preparation allowance` `the external exam is this year` `the school assessment is this year` IS
    `the subject's bagrut-preparation allowance`
        TIMES (  (IF `the external exam is this year` THEN `the external exam's share of the bagrut-preparation allowance` ELSE 0)
               + (IF `the school assessment is this year` THEN `the school assessment's share of the bagrut-preparation allowance` ELSE 0))

#ASSERT `the bagrut-preparation allowance paid this year, by §11(ה)` 1000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `the bagrut-preparation allowance paid this year, by §11(ה)` 1000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 1000

